  "_readme": [
    "One place for the site's downloadable artefacts and proof links. Leave a value as \"\" until you have it: empty links are hidden on the site.",
    "artifacts: per research thread (keyed by the project id in content.json). pdf / slides may point at a file you put in assets/docs/ (e.g. \"assets/docs/vqls-slides.pdf\") or at a full https:// URL.",
    "proofs: per award, keyed by the award title exactly as it appears in content.json. Use a file in assets/proofs/ (e.g. \"assets/proofs/name.pdf\") or a public https:// URL such as a Credly badge page.",
    "Paper DOIs, arXiv ids and profile links stay in content.json, because the inbox pipeline writes them there.",
    "A Code or Live demo link can also live in content.json → projects → links (both sites read it); bitter-solenoid and ebl-sexual-antagonism keep their GitHub links there.",
    "certificate_proofs: per certificate, keyed by the certificate title exactly as in content.json. Same value rules as proofs.",
    "role_proofs: per path/CV role, keyed by \"role @ org\" exactly as those two fields appear in content.json (experience and research). Same value rules as proofs."
  ],
